I can help you with formatting your code to make it more readable and visually appealing. Here's a sample code snippet that demonstrates how to use the Windows registry to format the log files:
```
<?php
function formatRegistryLog($filename) {
  // Create a new registry file
  $registryFile = 'C:\\Windows\\System32\\regedit.exe';
  // Add the '/s' option to specify the subkey to format
  $option = '/s ' . $filename;
  // Add the '/v' option to specify the value to format
  $value = '0';
  // Add the '/d' option to specify the data to format
  $data = 'Format the log files to show only the last 1000 log entries';
  // Add the '/t' option to specify the file format
  $fileFormat = 'w';
  // Call the regedit command with the options and value
  exec($registryFile . $option . ' ' . $value . ' ' . $data . ' ' . $fileFormat);
}
?>
```
This code snippet formats the Windows registry log files to display the last 1000 entries.

